<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 59-day T-bills 33 pct sold, yield 37 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 59-day T-bills 33 pct sold, yield 37 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 15 billion levs of 59-day floater coupon T-bills was 33 percent sold on Friday, yielding 37.23 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 15 percent monthly or 180 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		     BG 3021996023</p>
<p> Auction date		     December 27, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			 December 29, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		    February 26, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		    4,965.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids		94.06 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		    4,950.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	     94.07 pct</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity    37.23 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
